hexagon: a flash attention kernel whose softmax reads the HMX tiles as they are
Fold-into: upstream/hexagon-htp

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus the patches before this one in patches/series.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/flash-attn-ops.c  the kernel hmx_flash_attn_ext_v2 (HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX2): the
                                                softmax, the O update with the row sum, the Q load, the O
                                                store and the loop of the q blocks
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/flash-attn-ops.h  HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX2, the bit HTP_FA_OPT_TILE_SMX, the VTCM
                                                layout, the cost model and the plan search of the kernel
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/hmx-fa-kernels.h  hvx_vec_exp2_neg_f16
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp      the switch GGML_HEXAGON_FA_OPT, the shapes that go to the
                                                kernel, and its plan
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-opnode.h          the profile line of the kernel

The commit of this patch also adds the checks of hmx_flash_attn_ext_v2 to the DSP model of the hexhost
harness (tests/fuzz/hexhost/common/dsp_model.cpp).

The defect

In hmx_flash_attn_ext the HVX does the softmax of a KV block in three steps. It copies two rows at a time
from the S tiles into a row buffer of the thread. It calculates the maximum, exp2 and the row sum of each
row. Then it writes P into the P tiles. On the phone this phase takes 36.5 us for 320 rows by 1024 columns
(the phase trace of the stage sweep). The op of 1024 queries and 4096 KV rows has 208 such phases (13 q
blocks, 4 KV blocks, 4 KV heads), thus the softmax takes about 7.6 ms of the 13.0 ms of the op
(computed). While the HVX does the conversion and the softmax of a block, the HMX waits.

The change

1. The softmax reads the S tiles in the tile layout. One HVX vector of a 32x32 f16 tile holds two rows,
   with the values of the two rows interleaved for each column. Thus the maximum and exp2 operate on the
   tile vectors as they are, with no row buffer and no transpose. The mask goes into S in the same pass as
   the maximum. A mask value above -16 keeps its score, as in fa_softmax_impl. The softmax threads divide
   the row pairs of the q block.

2. hvx_vec_exp2_neg_f16 gives 2^-u with a polynomial of degree 3 with f16 coefficients. The integer part
   of u goes into the exponent field with a saturated subtraction. It has 15 HVX instructions.

3. The HMX calculates the row sum l: V gets one more column tile of ones, thus the O tile of that column
   holds l. The rescale of O by D = diag(2^(m_prev - m)) is one more tile MAC in the chain of the O
   update: the HMX multiplies D by O_prev, then adds P times V. The softmax writes only the diagonal of
   each D tile, with one predicated vscatter. The maximum m of each row stays in VTCM in f16.

4. The QK tiles come out of the HMX with the scale scale * log2(e), thus each QK score gets the scale of
   the op, and the softmax operates in base 2.

5. The O store divides each row by l. A row with l = 0 (each score of the row masked) gives 0, as the CPU
   backend gives.

6. The loop of the KV blocks is the pipeline of hmx_flash_attn_ext. The DMA runs two blocks ahead. At
   block b the HVX converts V(b) and K(b + 1) and does the softmax of b, while the HMX does the O update
   of b - 1 and the QK of b + 1. The mask of each block goes into a ring of 4 slots.

7. Between two q blocks, the Q load and the first QK of the next q block run while the HMX does the last
   O update of the current q block. With sinks, the Q load writes O[0], thus the next q block starts after
   the O store.

8. The thread of the op uses one DMA queue (the queue of thread 0) for Q, K, V and the masks, and the Q
   transfer of the next q block goes into the queue after the last pop of the current q block. The DMA
   engine of a hardware thread follows one descriptor chain: a push to a second queue while the engine
   works on the chain of the first queue never starts, and its pop waits forever. A candidate of this
   patch sent the next Q through the queue of thread 1. On the phone each op with transfers in flight
   on the two queues did not end (the stage fak, 2026-09-24: each real-model run of the kernel stopped
   at the kill of 110 s). The kernel lab did not find it, because its DMA shim copies at once. The lab
   target fa2 counts such pushes (full_dma_ring_violations): 14, 6 and 8 for three shapes of that
   candidate, 0 for this patch.

9. hmx_fa2_find_chunk_size selects Br and Bc with a cost model of the kernel (the constants of v79 in
   flash-attn-ops.h: the HMX tile, the work phase, the conversion of a row, the softmax of a tile vector
   and of a row pair, the Q preparation and the O store). The HVX terms divide over the threads and the
   HMX terms do not, thus the plan can change with the thread count. Another core needs its own
   constants.

10. The host selects HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX2 when the op is eligible for HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX, there is no logit
    softcap and no ALiBi, the mask is the same for each head (or there is no mask), DK equals DV, there is
    one KV row or more, and the Q rows times the GQA factor are 64 or more. The bit HTP_FA_OPT_TILE_SMX (1)
    of GGML_HEXAGON_FA_OPT enables the kernel (the preset value sets it). GGML_HEXAGON_FA_OPT=0 selects
    HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX for each shape, for an A/B run with one library set. The other shapes stay on
    HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX.

11. The kernel refuses kernel params whose Br, Bc, G, g_br and KV block count do not agree with the shapes
    (HTP_STATUS_INVAL_PARAMS).

12. The profile line of the op gives "hmx2-stream/BrxBc vtcm N".

The tests in the kernel lab (tools/htp-lab target fa2, v79, the release flags; measured)

- exp2: 10.2 cycles for each vector, against 24.6 for hvx_vec_exp2_f16. The maximum error over each f16
  value u in [0, 32] is 4.14 units in the last place (hvx_vec_exp2_f16: 4.42).
- One softmax step of 320 rows by 1024 columns: 131k cycles on 1 thread (fa_softmax_impl: 366k) and 48.6k
  cycles on 6 threads (fa_softmax_impl: 150k, thus 3.09 times less). 704 rows by 256 columns on 6
  threads: 3.0 times less.
- hmx_flash_attn_ext_v2 of this patch in the functional simulator against a reference in double, 16 and
  4 heads (or as given), head size 256 (or as given), 0 DMA queue violations:

      queries x KV rows    K and V   mask                    Br x Bc     NMSE
      200 x 300            Q8_0      causal, 2 q blocks      128 x 64    4.6e-7
      160 x 200            F16       none, 4 heads, G 1,     160 x 64    4.6e-7
                                     head size 64
      130 x 700            F16       values in [-1, 0]       48 x 256    5.2e-7
      100 x 250            F16       causal, 8/4 heads,      96 x 128    4.3e-7
                                     head size 128
      200 x 300            Q8_0      causal, sinks           128 x 64    1.3e-4

  Each run has 0 values that are not finite. With sinks the NMSE is larger: m holds the sink in f16, and
  when the sink is much larger than the scores, the f16 rounding of m - S changes P. HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX has
  the same property.

