Two defects of HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX that this patch does not change (found in the source, not reproduced):

- With a mask for each head (mask->ne[2] > 1), fa_push_mask_dma_gqa writes the mask of each KV block to
  the same address, vtcm_mask_buf. The transfer of the mask of block b + 1 starts before the softmax of
  block b reads its mask, thus the softmax can read the mask of the next block. The G mask rows of one
  q row also need G times the bytes of one slot of the mask buffer.
- A row with each score masked gives the row sum 0, and the O store divides by it. The output of such a
  row is not finite. HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX2 gives 0.

